      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Add a subtitle-template segment to the draft.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --resource TEXT     Subtitle template resource (vimo://<id>; local not supported)\r\n          --content TEXT      Slot content(s), pipe-separated, e.g. \"A|B\"\r\n          --start <duration>  Timeline start, e.g. 0s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or\r\n                              min; bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --duration <duration> \r\n                              Duration, e.g. 3s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or min;\r\n                              bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --keyword-range TEXT ... \r\n                              Keyword UTF-16 half-open range START,END; repeat for multiple\r\n                              keywords\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Add a subtitle-template segment from a resource id\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft subtitle template add --resource vimo://123\r\n  # Let the template resource style two keyword ranges\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft subtitle template add --resource vimo://123 --content \"Hello world\" --keyword-range 0,5 --keyword-range 6,11\r\n",
